'''Tukupi''' (from [[Kurupiran languages|Kuarupíba]] ''Tukũ-py''; {{Literal translation|water spirit}}) is a {{W|landlocked}} region in northern [[Araucaria]], and one of the [[regions of Balisca|eight regions of the community]]. It borders the [[Arapytúcaá]] region to the south, the [[Castejón|Castejón Metropolis]], [[Piedmont]], [[Luzamontaña]] and [[Vitacura]] to the east, and [[Jaguarundi]] to the north. It has an area of {{convert|32086 |km2|abbr=on}} making it the # largest region of Balisca, and a recorded population of 2,877,690 in the [[2025 Baliscan census|2025 census]]. 

The administrative center and most-populous city of Tukupi is [[Valparaíso]]. Tukupi is situated in a mountainous setting with vast greenery and lush vegetation, and is it part of [[Green Atlántida]]. The region has a [[W:Warm-summer Mediterranean climate|warm-summer Mediterranean climate]], characterized by warm, dry summers and cool to cold, winters. 

